'''Advanced Combat''' is a [[Fighting Styles|Fighting Style]] obtainable in the [[First Sea]], which serves as a direct successor to [[Combat]]. It has several time-based obtainment steps and a lot of random spawns, making it arguably the most time-consuming and the hardest fighting style to obtain in Blox Fruits across all seas.

==Obtainment==
# The player has to interact with the [[Secrets Master]] after completing all [[Island Secrets]] in the First Sea. That NPC will tell the player three stories when they choose the "Tell me some stories" option, each one describing an island.
# It should be able to, then, use the [[Middle Town]]'s teleporter to go to the islands in the order that the Secret Master gave. Afterward, the Middle Town's fountain water will turn off for the player, making the option at Secrets Master disappear.
# The teleporter must now be used to select the islands in the following order: [[Pirate Starter]] or [[Marine Starter]], [[Jungle]], [[Pirate Village]], [[Desert]], [[Frozen Village]], [[Marine Fortress]], [[Skylands|Lower Skylands]], [[Prison]], [[Colosseum (First Sea)|Colosseum]], [[Magma Village]], [[Underwater City]], [[Upper Skylands]], [[Fountain City]]. Then the user should teleport back to the Starter Island to receive the final secret and unlock access to the advanced combat puzzle.
# The player must now go to the [[Remove Blox Fruit]] NPC at the top of [[Prison]] to remove their fruit. Talk to the NPC again and select the new option: "Remove my Fighting Style". This will give the player the Combat fighting style.
# The player must defeat one of each [[Awakened Bosses|Awakened boss]] using [[Combat]] only, with each kill restoring parts of the fountain. After the fountain is restored back to normal, the Secrets Master will now be able to give Advanced Combat, as well as let the player swap back to Combat whenever they want.

Upon obtaining Advanced Combat, the player will receive the [[Titles|title]], {{Title|Class S|outline=1}} (#151).

==Tips==
* There is no level requirement for unlocking Advanced Combat besides the levels you earn from completing the Island Secrets.
** This also applies to all the steps mentioned above including talking the [[Remove Blox Fruit]] [[NPCs|NPC]].
* Server hopping or restarting a private server is recommended for completing the step for killing every awakened boss with Combat.
** Upper Skylands has 2 awakened bosses. You'll know which one awakens as they both have 2 different hints from the Secrets Master tied to their awakening minigame. Such as for Sky warlord, the secret master's hint is  "Forecast for a storm at Upper Skylands" while for Lightning god  "It's a beautiful day at Upper Skylands."
* [[Private Servers]] are recommended for completing time-based island secrets events as the player can choose which island an event will spawn on.
* The player can use [[Ghost]]'s "V" ability, [[Buddha]], [[Cyborg]] V3's [[Energy Core]], [[Angel]] V4's [[Angel|King's Rule]], and [[Draco]] V3's [[Flash Step]] passive to make killing each awakened boss significantly easier.
** The player can use Ghost's "V" to spawn clones that will also use Combat to deal damage, as long as the player is holding Combat out. The player must be careful to not swap to a [[Sword]] or [[Gun]], as the clones will start to use that instead, resulting in the attempt failing.
* Other players can help the player to kill the Awakened Bosses. As long as the player uses only Combat, the other players do not need to use Combat as well, although they won't get credit for Advanced Combat.

